@startuml
' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing the Episodes Act processing flow.
' Keep this diagram simple: a short linear flow with minimal partitions,
' one decision point, and explanatory notes instead of nested detail.


title Ghostwriter - Episodes Act Processing

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED

start

:Parse the act command;
note right
  Expands ">" shorthand, defaults to
  "help", splits act name from prompt,
  and reads episode selection like "#1,3!".
end note

:Load the act definition;
note right
  Merges built-in and custom TOML,
  resolves "basedOn" inheritance,
  and applies defaults and prompt values.
end note

:Find files to process;
note right
  If nothing matches, the project
  directory itself is processed.
end note

:Take next matching file;

if (Specific episodes were requested?) then (yes)
  :Begin with the selected episodes;
else (no)
  :Begin with episode 1;
endif

:Run the episode sequence;
note right
  Selected episodes run in the requested order.
  A trailing "!" ends processing for this file
  after those episodes; otherwise normal order continues.
end note

note right
  Each episode builds its prompt, resolves tools,
  and calls the AI provider. Its control signals can
  repeat an episode, jump to another one, or end this file.
end note

:Collect results and continue
with the next matching file;
note right
  When every matching file is complete,
  collect the overall results.
end note

stop

legend right
  * Episodes are ordered steps within one act.
  * A caller can select specific episodes and choose
    whether normal order continues afterward.
  * Control signals can repeat an episode, jump to another,
    or end the current file's processing.
endlegend
@enduml